+# KIO Grid full native fork
+
+Independent KIO branding fork of the complete Rust-native [GridCraft v0.7.0](https://github.com/storytold/gridcraft/releases/tag/v0.7.0), immutable commit `d9d09f0baa912e88c5111107903fc8c640214b57`. Based on GridCraft by the ArtCraft team. This is the entire native workspace, including all original engine, format, rendering, CLI, MCP and web modules. It is not the former simplified KIO web editor.
+
+## Scope and provenance
+
+The patch changes product/window/About labels, existing product-name translations, app/bundle/installer identity and the separate `com.kio.grid` preferences/recovery/log directory. Crate names, binary machine names, command IDs, file-format identifiers, dependency pins and internal built-in theme identifiers stay intact. The KIO icon is the existing supplied `public/kio-program-icons/grid.png` converted into platform formats. ArtCraft trademark mark/logo files and README logos are removed; their original trademark license is retained. MIT/Apache license files, NOTICE, contributor/model credits and all engine modules are byte-for-byte preserved. Original attribution is retained alongside KIO icon provenance. KIO is an independent fork, with no upstream endorsement.
+
+## Rebuild inputs
+
+[KIO-FORK.json](KIO-FORK.json) fixes the original archive SHA, icon SHA and `craft-fonts` input `abb83316d96aa59c1cf64784289e378fe9fa5695`. Use Rust 1.95 and the committed Cargo.lock. Set `CRAFT_FONTS_DIR` to the complete pinned font source and build the complete desktop and CLI packages: `cargo build --release --locked -p gridcraft -p gridcraft-cli`. A reusable binary Git patch and per-file before/after SHA manifest are provided beside the original source archive. Signing/notarization and binary QA are separate release steps.
+
+## Inherited limits
+
+Keeping every upstream feature does not establish Microsoft Excel parity. XLSX fidelity is not established with a real-world corpus. Some data-model/query-table/slicer content and chart options are not fully represented on save. Large-file/recalculation, formula-correctness, script/VBA and legacy-XLS restrictions remain as documented upstream. VBA projects may be preserved, but VBA execution is not supplied. See the preserved [upstream gaps](docs/gaps.md), [file-format parity](docs/file-format-parity.md), [localization parity](docs/localization-parity.md) and [target parity](docs/target-app-parity.md) for the complete pinned-release assessment. No gap is marked fixed by this branding patch.
+
+## Verification state
+
+This source patch is statically checked and reapplied to an independent extraction of the original archive. Protected engine, dependency, license and credit files are compared by SHA-256. The branding agent did not build, install or run an app. Native launch, About/icons, open/save, printing/export and recovery require the parent build/QA stage before release.
